NAME
    house - the PG-640A manual's house, animated

SYNOPSIS
    house [nf]

DESCRIPTION
    Draws the house from the Matrox PG-640A manual (the engine's
    reference design; docs/reference in the repo) as a 3D model and
    animates it: one full turn about its centre in nf frames (default
    72, five degrees a step), a 24-frame zoom out, a 24-frame zoom
    back in, and a straight-on resting frame.

    The house is recorded into GL command list 1 with its erase, FLIP
    and frame WAIT inside, so each animation step is one matrix delta
    plus CLRUN -- eight bytes a frame; the card does the rest. Works
    identically on the all-in-one build and across the bridge from
    runcard.sh: same bytes, same bus contract.

    The drawing is the manual's own worked example and is genuinely
    three-dimensional -- the flat look of the printed page is just its
    default viewpoint. List 1 is left recorded: gl MDROTY 30 CLRUN 1
    keeps playing with it.

SEE ALSO
    cube, gl, rotate, camera
